@startuml
hide empty description
state "calm" as calm {
  calm : intensity = calm_rate
}
state "active" as active {
  active : intensity = calm_rate * multiplier
}
state "pinned" as pinned {
  pinned : a state a person chose
}

[*] --> calm : the chain starts calm or active,\nseeded from the market stream
calm --> active : the chain draws a switch
active --> calm : the chain draws a switch
calm --> pinned : pin(state) from the Market tab or the shell
active --> pinned : pin(state)
pinned --> calm : pin(nothing): the chain resumes

state "the heat C(t), shared by every series" as heat
heat : every event of every series adds jump
heat : it fades at decay, so its gain is jump/decay
heat : a series takes the share of the heat its own rate is of the total
heat --> heat : an event raises the intensity\nand the intensity brings more events
note right of heat
  A Hawkes series adds its own self-excitation on top:
  a branching ratio and a decay per series, applied in
  that series' operational time. The heat is the market's;
  the branching ratio is the series'.
end note
heat -[dashed]-> calm : scales
heat -[dashed]-> active : scales
@enduml
